                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Immediate quick note: not exactly colorblind friendly, but not unplayable, just a bit more trial-and-error.\r\n\r\nSo I originally was drawn to the beautiful artstyle and the abstract puzzle genre has always appealed to me.\r\nWhile the game absolutely is a great and unique puzzle experience, I was more surprised by the actual story in the game.\r\nSimple, cute and straightforward, but I will say, it did make me want to complete the puzzles a bit more rapidly, so I could see the events.\r\nSo kudos to the developer for an effective story in short, with little dialogue and a lot of implications and story vignettes.\r\n\r\nOn the actual gameplay side, this game has a TON of leniency for solutions and the lovely feature that is quite difficult for many games to accomplish\r\nWhich is that the puzzles have multitude of solutions and a lot of possibilities.\r\nNow granted, it comes at the expense of the puzzles being a little bit more on the easier side, but in my mind, they are not too easy.\r\n\r\nI enjoyed my time with the game quite a bit. While I did have to do a couple tries on many of the later puzzle, the progression was fantastic.\r\n\r\nThe audio side is also surprisingly positive. The background music has an excellent vibe for the game.\r\nIt is contemplative, but adventurous and dreamlike. Perfect for the purpose.\r\n\r\nAll in all, surprisingly far more than the sum of its parts. Very solid puzzle game with a unique feel to it.",
